<title>USA: Boeing says Maersk Air orders two 737s.</title>
<headline>Boeing says Maersk Air orders two 737s.</headline>
<dateline>SEATTLE 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Maersk Air Group and Boeing Co said Maersk ordered two Boeing 737-500 twinjets valued at $72 million.</p>
<p>Deliveries are scheduled for September and October 1998. Copenhagen-based Maersk Air's fleet currently consists of 30 Boeing 737s.</p>
<p>Maersk also is the European launch customer for the next-generation 737-700. The airline placed an order for 12 737-700s in 1994, the first of which will be delivered this year.</p>
</text>
